{"id":"3a870504ed2ae0cf","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-thm-deligne-weil-i.md","title":"Deligne Purity (Weil I)","display":"thm-deligne-weil-i — Deligne Purity (Weil I)","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-deligne-weil-i","aliases":["58-thm-deligne-weil-i","Deligne Purity Theorem"],"display":"thm-deligne-weil-i — Deligne Purity (Weil I)","depends_on":["[[58-df-finite-field-projective-variety]]","[[58-df-field]]","[[58-df-prime-number]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-deligne-weil-i"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-deligne-weil-i</span><span>Deligne Purity Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-deligne-weil-i — Deligne Purity (Weil I)"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e85b3308cfc79da5\" href=\"?note=e85b3308cfc79da5\" title=\"58-df-finite-field-projective-variety\">58-df-finite-field-projective-variety</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1eb4a89b005d9cda\" href=\"?note=1eb4a89b005d9cda\" title=\"58-df-field\">58-df-field</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"58-df-prime-number\">58-df-prime-number</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\ell\">\\(\\ell\\)</span> are distinct primes, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"q=p^r\">\\(q=p^r\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> is a smooth projective variety of dimension <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"d\">\\(d\\)</span> over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb F_q\">\\(\\mathbb F_q\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H^i_{\\acute e t}(X_{\\overline{\\mathbb F}_q},\\mathbb Q_\\ell)\">\\(H^i_{\\acute e t}(X_{\\overline{\\mathbb F}_q},\\mathbb Q_\\ell)\\)</span> is the finite-dimensional etale cohomology space and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F_{X,i}^*\">\\(F_{X,i}^*\\)</span> is geometric Frobenius on degree <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"i\">\\(i\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\">\\(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\">\\(\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\)</span> are fixed algebraic closures. A field embedding <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\iota_\\ell:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\">\\(\\iota_\\ell:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\)</span> identifies algebraic-number representatives of Frobenius eigenvalues.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SmoothProjectiveVarietyOver}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{SmoothProjectiveVarietyOver}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S\\)</span> are supplied by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e85b3308cfc79da5\" href=\"?note=e85b3308cfc79da5\" title=\"58-df-finite-field-projective-variety\">58-df-finite-field-projective-variety</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Prime}\">\\(\\mathrm{Prime}\\)</span> is the exact prime-number predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"dad686059f3ca152\" href=\"?note=dad686059f3ca152\" title=\"58-df-prime-number\">58-df-prime-number</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}deligne\\text{-}weil\\text{-}i}\\vdash\n\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land\\mathrm{Prime}(\\ell)\\land p\\neq\\ell\\land\nr\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land q=p^r\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S(\\mathbb F_q,q)\\land\\mathrm{SmoothProjectiveVarietyOver}_S(X,\\mathbb F_q,q,d)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\n\\to\\exists\\iota_\\ell:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\;\n\\forall i\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\;\\left[\n\\det\\!\\left(\\beta I-F_{X,i}^*\\right)=0\\to\n\\exists\\alpha\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\;\\left(\n\\iota_\\ell(\\alpha)=\\beta\\land\n\\forall\\iota_\\infty:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\mathbb C\\;\n|\\iota_\\infty(\\alpha)|=q^{i/2}\\right)\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}deligne\\text{-}weil\\text{-}i}\\vdash\n\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land\\mathrm{Prime}(\\ell)\\land p\\neq\\ell\\land\nr\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land q=p^r\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S(\\mathbb F_q,q)\\land\\mathrm{SmoothProjectiveVarietyOver}_S(X,\\mathbb F_q,q,d)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\n\\to\\exists\\iota_\\ell:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\;\n\\forall i\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\;\\left[\n\\det\\!\\left(\\beta I-F_{X,i}^*\\right)=0\\to\n\\exists\\alpha\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\;\\left(\n\\iota_\\ell(\\alpha)=\\beta\\land\n\\forall\\iota_\\infty:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\mathbb C\\;\n|\\iota_\\infty(\\alpha)|=q^{i/2}\\right)\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The conclusion separates the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\ell\">\\(\\ell\\)</span>-adic realization from the complex embeddings: every geometric-Frobenius eigenvalue is represented by an algebraic number, and every complex conjugate of that algebraic number has absolute value <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"q^{i/2}\">\\(q^{i/2}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Rationality, the functional equation, and the trace formula are not folded into this purity assertion.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Deligne, La conjecture de Weil I, Publications Mathématiques de l'IHÉS 43 (1974)</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-finite-field-projective-variety","status":"resolved","id":"e85b3308cfc79da5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-finite-field-projective-variety]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-field","status":"resolved","id":"1eb4a89b005d9cda","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-field]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-prime-number","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-prime-number]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-finite-field-projective-variety","status":"resolved","id":"e85b3308cfc79da5","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{SmoothProjectiveVarietyOver}_S$ and $\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S$ are supplied by [[58-df-finite-field-projective-variety]].","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-prime-number","status":"resolved","id":"dad686059f3ca152","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Prime}$ is the exact prime-number predicate from [[58-df-prime-number]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"p","display":false},{"tex":"\\ell","display":false},{"tex":"r\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"q=p^r","display":false},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"d","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb F_q","display":false},{"tex":"H^i_{\\acute e t}(X_{\\overline{\\mathbb F}_q},\\mathbb Q_\\ell)","display":false},{"tex":"F_{X,i}^*","display":false},{"tex":"i","display":false},{"tex":"\\overline{\\mathbb Q}","display":false},{"tex":"\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell","display":false},{"tex":"\\iota_\\ell:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SmoothProjectiveVarietyOver}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Prime}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}deligne\\text{-}weil\\text{-}i}\\vdash\n\\left[\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{Prime}(p)\\land\\mathrm{Prime}(\\ell)\\land p\\neq\\ell\\land\nr\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land q=p^r\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{FiniteField}_S(\\mathbb F_q,q)\\land\\mathrm{SmoothProjectiveVarietyOver}_S(X,\\mathbb F_q,q,d)\n\\end{aligned}\\right]\n\\to\\exists\\iota_\\ell:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\;\n\\forall i\\in\\omega\\;\\forall\\beta\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}_\\ell\\;\\left[\n\\det\\!\\left(\\beta I-F_{X,i}^*\\right)=0\\to\n\\exists\\alpha\\in\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\;\\left(\n\\iota_\\ell(\\alpha)=\\beta\\land\n\\forall\\iota_\\infty:\\overline{\\mathbb Q}\\hookrightarrow\\mathbb C\\;\n|\\iota_\\infty(\\alpha)|=q^{i/2}\\right)\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"\\ell","display":false},{"tex":"q^{i/2}","display":false}],"bytes":2343,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4109","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-thm-deligne-weil-i.md|58-thm-deligne-weil-i]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["e85b3308cfc79da5","1eb4a89b005d9cda","dad686059f3ca152"]}